{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1042318-africa","id":1042318,"title":"Africa?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-02T03:08:57-08:00","id":1042318,"title":"Africa?","content":"A quick question before going to work:<br /> <br /> I like Mage but I'm sorely lacking in practical knowledge about it. I'm now working on an African setting and I'd like to know if there's some material I can use as a starting point. Can you please list what we know about Africa in Mage terms? Magical traditions, Nameless Orders, peculiarities and pretty much everything else: I could use anything there is. The setting I'm writing is a localized one, but inspiration sources are always welcome.<br /> <br /> I guess the Mutapa Empire Dark Era will help in this regard, but in the meantime, what we already know?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T06:49:36-08:00","id":1042384,"title":"","content":"From what I know, there isn't many more than paragraph or two about Africa in each Order book - but I could missed something...<br /> <br /> Oh, wait - there IS something - in 1E <b>Magical Traditions</b> book you have Santerie and Appalachian Hoodoo - both with roots in Africa. I assume that remaking them in to Nameless Orders would not be that hard thing to do. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T06:51:55-08:00","id":1042385,"title":"","content":"Define &quot;Africa&quot;. As I've said before here, Africa is a continent; it could contain the United States, China, and Europe, and still have room for three Great Britains to spare.<br /> <br /> Africa is a truly staggeringly huge place and that hugeness is represented in diversity. No two places are the same; not in politics, history, religion, culture...<br /> <br /> Figure out where you're going to put your game first, then do some research on that area. The rest will usually come on its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T07:13:43-08:00","id":1042395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1042318-africa?p=1042385#post1042385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Define &quot;Africa&quot;. As I've said before here, Africa is a continent; it could contain the United States, China, and Europe, and still have room for three Great Britains to spare.<br /> <br /> Africa is a truly staggeringly huge place and that hugeness is represented in diversity. No two places are the same; not in politics, history, religion, culture...<br /> <br /> Figure out where you're going to put your game first, then do some research on that area. The rest will usually come on its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that well and I said the same thing myself many times. But, as I've stated, in the opening post I am honestly looking for everything we got about the whole continent.<br /> <br /> I'm writing about Congo. I've been reading my books, made my research and I have a list of ideas. Read about Bantu myths, regional folklore and stuff. But since material tends to be sparse, I'm looking for potential tidbits of informations or ideas from what we canonically have so far. Again, as I wrote, I recognize it might not be about related what I'm writing, but it's better than starting completely from scratch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T07:28:11-08:00","id":1042404,"title":"","content":"I think Seers of the Throne has a section on what that order is doing on each continent, and the Africa subheading is the standard &quot;war! genocide! horror! oh the humanity!&quot; that you would expect from an unfamiliar writer. It doesn't have any real specifics from what I remember, except that the Praetorian Ministry is strong there. <br /> <br /> Secrets of the Ruined Temple has a pretty interesting hook in the world history chapter: in the present day, there's a growing Christian-derived movement on that continent that sees Atlantis in a radically different way, as a future ideal to be achieved and realized on Earth rather than a lost empire and cautionary tale of the past. There's probably some stuff about Timbuktu in that book too, I don't remember offhand.<br /> <br /> edit: if you're setting it in Congo, the Katanga Crisis was 100% a Praetorian op to create their own territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T07:32:17-08:00","id":1042407,"title":"","content":"I do realize the opening post was written quickly and might be misleading, but I'm making no assumptions about Africa, I'm not conflating the whole immense place and its hundreds cultures into a single one and I'm fully aware that doing so would be blatantly wrong. It's for similar reasons I never liked the idea of &quot;African&quot; or &quot;North American&quot; pantheon in Scion.<br /> <br /> I've got that covered, don't worry.<br /> <br /> But I asked for something else. I had trouble finding Mage material that gives us information about any African culture aside from Egypt. Not saying there's not, just that I don't know where to look. <br /> <br /> Apologies if that was not clear or it looked like I was making a wrong statement up there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T08:22:57-08:00","id":1042427,"title":"","content":"I did some digging, and the stuff in the Order books is a little better than I remembered. Most of it is pretty general, but there are a few ideas that could be a starting point for building a regional Consilium. Mysterium and Seers of the Throne are especially good IMO. If you have them as PDFs, I suggest you ctrl+F &quot;Africa&quot; and see what comes up. Same thing for Secrets of the Ruined Temple, there's some good stuff in there, and not just from a European explorer's perspective.<br /> <br /> NB: the word &quot;Africa&quot; or related information doesn't appear even once in Free Council, black sheep of the Order books, but this pic is always relevant<br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/fdDLyod.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T08:28:08-08:00","id":1042431,"title":"","content":"As I just was looking over <b>Secrets of the Ruined Temple</b>, I remembered other tibits about Time Before civilization in Africa. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SotRT, p. 23</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Something New Out of Africa</i><br /> Aristeas was only one of the earliest Awakened Seekers among the Greeks to voyage far over the horizon in search of Atlantis. A Sardinian willworker sailed north to icy seas with Pytheas; a Trapeziote mage explored djinn-haunted caves in southern Arabia, and not a few followed the tracks of the Egyptians into the desert. <br /> Here, they met the Garamanteans, red-haired, chariot-driving warriors with black skins who lived in the Fezzan Desert deep in Libya and resembled a blend \u2014 or an ancestor? \u2014 of all hu-manity. The Garamanteans\u2019 gardens in the empty Sahara had a de\ufb01nite \ufb02avor of the Hyperborean about them, paradises in the wasteland. The gardens bloomed in all seasons, watered by wells and underground aqueducts cut unguessable centuries before. <br /> Some Mysterium scholars followed Garamantean priests deep into those tunnels beneath the desert, seeking the \u201cinner ocean\u201d from which the Garamantean legends claimed the Garamanteans emerged millennia ago. During the chaos of Rome\u2019s fall, the Garamantean kingdom vanished under Vandal raids and epic sandstorms. The Garamanteans left behind desiccating vineyards of unknown vintage, from the shriveled produce of which some Berber tribes de\ufb01antly distill the potent Syrah Atlantide served at a few very exclusive Silver Ladder banquets. The dreams it grants are said to be evocative in the extreme.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T08:32:50-08:00","id":1042434,"title":"","content":"As to Congo proper - I would advise to make local Nameless Order. But to do this, we need to asses what would look like it's 'shamanistic caste' in myths and tales of Congo indigenous people. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar38_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"38\" data-vbnamecard=\"38\">Cinder</a>, do you know anything about magical/shamanistic traditions of the region? If yes, maybe do us a small essey here, so we could help you better? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T07:53:28-08:00","id":1042946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1042318-africa?p=1042434#post1042434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to Congo proper - I would advise to make local Nameless Order. But to do this, we need to asses what would look like it's 'shamanistic caste' in myths and tales of Congo indigenous people. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar38_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"38\" data-vbnamecard=\"38\">Cinder</a>, do you know anything about magical/shamanistic traditions of the region? If yes, maybe do us a small essey here, so we could help you better? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not easy, since Congo is huge and there are many different cultures in it, but going by broad strokes you can find some common points that can be used for Mage. The ones I try to keep in mind are:<br /> <br /> - Ancestors are the basis of most of the beliefs. There are also natural spirits and you can converse with animals, but the cult of the ancestors is the core of the religion. You try to contact your ancestors for protection and when something bad happens it might easily be because a dead one take offense for something the living did.<br /> <br /> - There's often the idea of a Supreme God, but there's no common agreement on what it is. Often the First Ancestor that founded a tribe, sometimes an entity related to the Sun or the Moon. Many myths tend to point out two things. First, that God did not necessarily made people or the animals, simply that it is &quot;greater. Second, that it used to live in the world but left for some reason, the one most often cited is because men did something wrong.<br /> <br /> - Both Heaven and the Land of the Dead are places that can be visited. Not surprisingly, considering the focus of the ancestors, the Underworld comes up way more frequently. It kinda aligns with cthonic myths from around the world, with the dead merely living their &quot;unlife&quot; there, their food and items something the living must not take and the place being generally dark and gloomy, but not intrinsecally &quot;bad&quot;. Heaven, on the other hand, has its population too, but they are &quot;weird&quot; people of unspecified nature or heavenly animals. A good rule to travel in both worlds is to listen to what people say, be respectful and don't break the rules.<br /> <br /> - A very Mage-like notion is that in the ancient times people used to be able to travel to Heaven more freely in the past, either by using a cord or climbing a tree. The point is that they were not exactly supposed to and, at a certain point, the entrance was barred, the cord or the trees cut down and the People Above became way more difficult to contact. It's not an universal myth, but it's common enough and has too many Mage parallels to not use.<br /> <br /> - Death was not a thing from the start. The details vary but in general the story goes this way: God sends both a chameleon and a lizard to give a message to mankind. The chameleon's message is &quot;You will never die&quot;, the lizard one is the opposite. The chameleon, either because of laziness or carelessness, wastes time along the way and lizard arrives first. When the chameleon gives its message to mankind it's too late because people have already accepted the idea of Death. It's also the reason why lizards and chameleons are considered unlucky animals (the chameleon especially because screw that guy)<br /> <br /> - Symbolism, especially related to items and fetishes, means a damn lot. There's power in items and you can bind spirits, both natural and ancestral ones to them.<br /> <br /> - The term &quot;doctor&quot; can be used as synonymous for Mage without much issues. It's the general term for &quot;person with knowledge&quot; and in legends it often comes with knowledge about the supernatural as well.<br /> <br /> That's what I can recall without going too much specific.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T09:03:31-08:00","id":1042977,"title":"","content":"Okay, here is how I would roll with the setting like this :<br /> <br /> 1. Many believes, many Nameless Orders - no one said that you must stick to only one as particular character. <br /> 2. Nameless Orders should be - on general - only a bit wider than Legacy philosophy. From what you say we should have at least two in Congo - one to Ancestors, other focused on Heaven. <br /> 3. Ancestors are like human progenitors of each family - or like animal totems that guide each tribe? If first - based them on ghost and Underworld. If second - it basically works like in Australia, so use my proposed Dreamspeakers Order. <br /> 4. Heaven in myths sounds more like Changeling Arcadia or like Supernal Realms? If the second, use specific created Emanating Realm, like Mists for Supernal Arcadia from 2E Mage. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-03-2017, 12:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T09:59:53-08:00","id":1043011,"title":"","content":"Note that, where there are prominent Nameless Orders, there too may be the Free Council, which could be useful for consolidating numerous regional magical traditions into a single political and social framework. Perhaps local Orders decided to throw in their lot because elements of the Seers and the Diamond Orders aligned with the colonial elite were running roughshod over the Congolese Nameless in order to gain converts to their respective philosophies and appropriate local mysteries for their own purposes. <br /> <br /> You could even have an emerging political divide between local mages who see continued benefit in their allegiance to the Council, while others, even from the same sub-orders, see that allegiance as an unwanted vestige of colonialism and prefer to chart their own independent course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 02-03-2017, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T12:20:12-08:00","id":1043082,"title":"","content":"Cinder writes about his Dark Eras setting for colonial Congo, way before creation of Free Council. Also, not always Free Council = local Nameless Orders - there are higher chances on that, but Nameless could still not to join Assemblies. Or even they can help Seers, if they are sold good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T12:29:10-08:00","id":1043086,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna use that for a Congo Free State Dark Era, but I left the thread unspecified because here I'm looking for more general ideas, not specifically related to any time period.<br /> <br /> All is good, since knowing what could have been the situation even before or after the time window I'm interested about can prove useful","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T21:22:21-08:00","id":1043365,"title":"","content":"So Cinder, you need to answer my questions if you want our help. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T0